<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Castle Rock, Edinburgh</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Castle Rock is the volcanic plug in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a> on which Edinburgh Castle stands. Occupied since the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a>, it is identified with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/din-eidyn">Din Eidyn</a>, the stronghold of the British kingdom of Gododdin that fell to Northumbria in the 7th century, and it later became a royal castle of the Scottish kings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/castle-rock-edinburgh.jpg" alt="Castle Rock, Edinburgh" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kim Traynor · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Castle_from_Princes_Street,_Edinburgh.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
